  "provenance": {
    "source": "the catalog's source 9, a liquid drum and bass tune (mining id 9)",
    "reading": "NMF decomposition of the full mix against the tune's own drum one-shots (percussive part averaged on the grid), read at every sixteenth of the first groove (16 bars) and the first drop (32 bars)",
    "knowledge": "mined: per lane and step of a two-bar cycle, how often it plays, how loud (over the lane's loudest), the spread, and its median offset; no audio kept",
    "note": "kick on 1 and the and-of-3; the snare soft on 2, loud on 4; a drag ghost a sixteenth before each snare; a bright hat on 3, a soft hat ticking with its accent after the downbeat; an open hat into every second downbeat",
    "moved": "revision 3 (the review of 10-08, B5): the open lane plays the open hat (hatOpen); it played the soft hat, so each of its hits doubled or flammed a soft-hat hit and none rang open; revision 4 (liquid-space, 10-11): answers (the end of one bar changed, by a phrase's plan) and states (half-time, hints, pulse: other bars the kit plays, a full set of lanes each), authored from the territory's conventions; the lanes, sections, lift, phrase fill and moves of revision 3 unchanged"
  }
